const FAQ_ITEMS = [
  ["What is Glasto Quick Copy?", "A free, unofficial helper for Glastonbury ticket day. It puts your group's registration numbers and postcodes on one page so you can copy each one with a tap instead of typing or scrolling through messages."],
  ["Is this the official Glastonbury website?", "No. We're an independent project, not connected to Glastonbury Festival or See Tickets. You still register and buy tickets on the official sites."],
  ["Does it get me tickets faster?", "It can't speed up the queue. It saves time once you're through, when you need to enter up to six registration numbers and postcodes quickly and accurately."],
  ["Is it free?", "Yes. The tool and guides are free, paid for by ads from Google."],
  ["Where are my group's details stored?", "In your browser's storage on your own device. The tool has no accounts and no database, and its code never sends your group's details anywhere. Groups and links are cleared on a seasonal schedule: details created from June through October are cleared on 1 December; details created from November through May are cleared on 1 June. Like any site with ads, Google's ad code runs on these pages. See our [privacy and cookies policy](/privacy/)."],
  ["Can other people see my group's numbers?", "Only people you send the share link to. The link contains first names, registration numbers and postcodes, and anyone with the link can read them, so share it only with your group."],
  ["How many people can I add?", "Up to six, the maximum one lead booker can buy for in a single Glastonbury booking."],
  ["Who needs to register for Glastonbury?", "Everyone who will be 13 or over when the gates open. Children aged 12 and under don't need a ticket or a registration. See [how registration works](/guides/how-glastonbury-registration-works/)."],
  ["Are there separate tickets for people with access needs?", "No. Everyone books in the same sales, then applies for access facilities afterwards. For 2027 the application form link is available from the end of November 2026. See [access requirements](/guides/glastonbury-access-requirements/)."],
  ["What do I need for each person on ticket day?", "Their registration number and the postcode they registered with."],
  ["I've lost my registration number. What now?", "Use the official registration lookup on See Tickets with the email address you registered with, and your number will be emailed to you again."],
  ["How long does photo approval take?", "The festival says photos are reviewed within about 48 hours in the working week. If you hear nothing within a further 48 hours, register again."],
  ["Can I change my registration photo after booking?", "Not while a booking is linked to your registration, so update an old photo before ticket day."],
  ["Do extra tabs or devices help in the queue?", "In recent sales, no. For 2027 you entered your registration details before joining the queue, and one registration meant one place, so extra tabs on the same registration gave the same place. The official advice is also not to refresh or use several devices. See [how the queue works](/guides/how-the-ticket-queue-works/)."],
  ["Is there a trick to getting Glastonbury tickets?", "No. Since the 2027 sale, each registration gets one place in the queue, so extra tabs and devices don't help. What does help is more people in your group queueing with their own registration, and everyone's details ready to paste so a place isn't wasted. See [how to get Glastonbury tickets](/guides/how-to-get-glastonbury-tickets/)."],
  ["How long do I have once I'm through the queue?", "In the 2025 sale it was 10 minutes to complete the page with everyone's registration details, and reports said the payment page then had its own, shorter timer. Tickets weren't allocated until payment went through, so have every registration number and postcode ready to paste. See [paying for Glastonbury tickets](/guides/paying-for-glastonbury-tickets/)."],
  ["How fast do Glastonbury tickets sell out?", "In under an hour every recent year: about 57 minutes for 2024, 35 for 2025 and 42 for 2027. See [recent sales compared](/guides/glastonbury-ticket-sale-history/)."],
  ["How much is the deposit?", "In the 2027 sale it was £100 per ticket, on a £408 ticket. The £308 balance, plus postage, is due between 1 and 7 April 2027. See [deposits and balances](/guides/deposits-and-balance-payments/)."],
  ["What if someone in my group can't pay the balance?", "If the balance isn't paid by the end of the window, that ticket is cancelled and goes into the spring resale. In 2025 the deposit was refunded to the original card minus a £25 administration fee."],
  ["Can I give my ticket to a friend?", "No. Glastonbury tickets carry the holder's photo and are non-transferable. Returned tickets are sold again only through the official resale."],
  ["Is there a resale?", "Usually, in late April, for tickets that weren't fully paid for or were returned. In 2025 you could book up to four general admission tickets or two coach packages, paid in full. The 2027 date hasn't been announced. See [how the resale works](/guides/resale-and-coach-tickets/)."],
  ["When is Glastonbury 2027?", "Wednesday 23 to Sunday 27 June 2027. Tickets went on sale in October 2026 and sold out. See [2027 key dates](/guides/glastonbury-2027-key-dates/)."],
  ["Do children need a ticket?", "Only if they'll be 13 or over on the day the gates open. For 2027 that's anyone born on or before 23 June 2014. See [taking children to Glastonbury](/guides/glastonbury-with-children/)."],
  ["Does the tool work on iPhone and Android?", "Yes, in any modern browser. Copying uses your browser's clipboard. If copying fails, the box says so: tap it to try again, or type the number in from the screen."],
  ["What does Keep screen on do?", "It asks your browser to stop the screen locking while your group's page is open, if your browser supports it. It switches off when you leave the page."],
  ["How do I delete my data?", "In the tool, open How your data is handled and choose Delete everything on this phone. Clearing your browser's site data also removes it."],
  ["Who makes this?", "A product manager, not a professional developer, who got fed up scrolling the group chat for numbers every ticket day. See [About](/about/)."],
];

